# eliza/psyche/ is GENERATED by tools/publicize.py from PUBLIC_MANIFEST.json.
# Committing it would create a second copy of the source that drifts silently:
# a fix applied to the copy passes local tests and disappears on the next
# materialise. The CI workflow materialises before installing.
/eliza/

# The Kali mirror (adopted/kali/) is vendored by tools/adopt_queue.py --vendor, and
# adopted/src is a junction to it so Kali's own root detection finds <root>/src.
# Both are rebuildable: one command from the recorded source, never hand-edited.
/adopted/kali/
/adopted/src

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.requiem/
